invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser_ext.c
catches: srv_test
reason: take_share holds a key_exchange to at least its group's length
  rather than exactly that many, so a 33-byte x25519 share, a 1217-byte
  X25519MLKEM768 share or a 66-byte secp256r1 point is handed to the key
  exchange, which reads the length it expects and agrees on a key the
  client computed from different bytes. srv_parser.h fixes each length,
  and test/srv_parser_tests.h requires illegal_parameter one byte over it
  as well as one byte under, for every group.

--- old
    if (share_len != share_len_of(bit)) {
--- new
    if (share_len < share_len_of(bit)) {
